 ```
 
 A projection is `*`, `alias.*`, or an expression with an optional `AS name`
 (the `AS` may be omitted). `FROM` is required.
 
+## Set operations
+
+`UNION`, `INTERSECT`, and `EXCEPT` may be chained after a `SELECT`.  Each
+accepts an optional `ALL` qualifier.  Both sides must produce the same number
+of columns; output column names come from the left side, and pairwise types
+are unified exactly as `UNION` unifies them.  Two rows are considered equal
+when every column matches by value **and** by type after both sides have been
+cast to the unified types, so integer `1` and float `1.0` are equal once the
+column type is resolved to `float64`.  Two `NULL` values are treated as equal,
+unlike a `=` comparison between them.
+
+**`UNION`** — concatenates both inputs.  Without `ALL`, duplicate rows are
+removed; with `ALL` every row from both sides appears.
+
+**`INTERSECT`** — keeps rows that appear in both inputs.  Without `ALL` each
+surviving row appears once; with `ALL` a row that appears *m* times on the
+left and *n* times on the right survives `min(m, n)` times.
+
+**`EXCEPT`** — keeps left rows that the right side never produced.  Without
+`ALL` each surviving row appears once; with `ALL` a row that appears *m* times
+on the left and *n* times on the right survives `max(m − n, 0)` times, with
+each right-hand copy cancelling the earliest left-hand copy still standing.
+
+Output order follows the left-hand input.  `ORDER BY`, `LIMIT`, and `OFFSET`
+written after the last `SELECT` in a chain apply to the combined result and
+are keyed on the combined output column names.
+
+### Precedence
+
+`INTERSECT` binds more tightly than `UNION` and `EXCEPT`, which sit at the
+same level and associate left-to-right:
+
+| Expression | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `a UNION b INTERSECT c` | `a UNION (b INTERSECT c)` |
+| `a EXCEPT b EXCEPT c` | `(a EXCEPT b) EXCEPT c` |
+
